{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>In the morning and He will know, etc.</b> The reason he said ״in the morning״ and so forth and did not perform the test at that very time — perhaps because the incense offering of בֵּין הָעַרְבַּיִם, in which the test takes place, had already been offered. Further, so that they would not suspect him of performing the test at an unfitting time, namely בֵּין הָעַרְבַּיִם, which is not a time of goodwill, as our Sages of blessed memory said in the holy Zohar (Zohar vol. 2, 39a) that it is a time when the forces of judgment prevail. Further, the man of Elohim intended by this to give them the nighttime to reflect on their deeds — perhaps they would recognize that they were not doing well and return in repentance. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 18:7) other reasons why he delayed until morning; these and those are the words of the living Elohim." "<b>him who is His and the holy one, etc.</b> One needs to know why he repeated, saying <b>him who is His and the holy one</b>. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Zohar, Numbers 176b): ״אֲשֶׁר לוֹ״ — this is the Levite service; ״הַקָּדוֹשׁ״ — this is the priesthood. And one needs to know why it was necessary to mention the matter of the Levite service, since they protested only about the priesthood. And according to what I have explained, that Korah took the princes of the tribe of Reuben with him in his claim that the greatness should revert to the firstborn among the brothers, therefore he was compelled to respond also regarding this division." "<b>Further,</b> it may be explained by raising yet another question: why did he repeat, saying <b>and him whom He chooses He will bring near to Him</b>? It further intends the following: since in their protest there are two aspects — the first, that Aaron is not so worthy, for among them there are greater and better men than he; and the second, that there exist men like him among the people who are fit to stand and minister alongside him. Therefore, corresponding to what pertains to Aaron's priesthood, that there is one more worthy than he, he said <b>him who is His</b> — meaning, who was designated for His service from the beginning of Creation, along the lines of what He said (Jeremiah 1:5): ״בְּטֶרֶם אֶצָּרְךָ בַבֶּטֶן״, etc. — <b>and the holy one</b> means: after he came into the world, he sanctified himself and made himself a vessel fit to minister in the holy. And he was precise in saying <b>and He brought near</b>, to hint that He had already brought him near and caused His Shekhinah to rest upon his hand. And corresponding to what was understood from them, that their intention was to add others alongside him, he said <b>and him whom He chooses He will bring near to Him</b> — if there are men as worthy as Aaron to stand as well and minister, He will bring near to Him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:05.263740193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}